    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Professor-Associate-or-Assistant-Professor-%28tenure-track%29-in-Geology-and-Mineralogy/1370974557/": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate or Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Geology and Mineralogy",
      "description": "Professor / Associate or Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Geology and Mineralogy Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Professor / Associate or Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Geology and Mineralogy The Department of Geosciences and Geography, in the Faculty of Science, invites applications for a PROFESSOR / ASSISTANT or ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR (TENURE TRACK) IN GEOLOGY AND MINERALOGY The position may be filled either as a permanent Professorship or as a fixed-term Assistant or Associate Professorship (tenure track), depending on the qualifications and career stage of the selected candidate. Further information about the University of Helsinki tenure track system is available on the university's website . Job Description The purpose of the professorship is to complement the department's research and teaching activities and to promote development of the appointee’s research area in close collaboration with the research groups in environmental and high temperature geochemistry, critical mineral systems and with the Institute of Seismology. The successful applicant is expected to build a research group and to lead international collaborative projects within their field. Suitable research focus areas include, but are not limited to, spatial and temporal aspects of igneous and hydrothermal processes and water- and melt-rock reactions applicable to Precambrian bedrock. The candidate is expected to establish active research collaborations with national and international research institutions as well as the industry and the public sector. The candidate is expected to utilize and further develop the department’s HelLabs infrastructure . The appointee will participate in teaching and supervision at all levels within the department and will develop study materials focused on mineralogy and petrology with a particular emphasis on Finnish bedrock geology within the BSc Programme in Geosciences and MSc Programme in Geology and Geophysics. Responsibilities include teaching in Finnish in the BSs programme in Geosciences and in English in the MSc Programme in Geology and Geophysics. Selection Criteria To be successful in the position, the applicant shall develop/have a strong collaborative international network, and a demonstrated ability to conduct research on an internationally high level as well as take advantage of national and international research funding opportunities. The appointee will participate in teaching and supervision at all levels in the department and develop study materials focused on mineralogy and petrology with a particular emphasis on Finnish bedrock geology within the BSc Programme in Geosciences and MSc Programme in Geology and Geophysics. Hence, expertise in these topics and proven teaching experience will be considered advantageous. Candidates appointed as Assistant or Associate Professors must hold a doctoral degree and demonstrate the ability to conduct independent scholarly work as well as possess the teaching skills required for the position. They must also demonstrate, through publications and other achievements, both the ability and motivation for an academic career, along with the ability or potential to obtain external research funding and lead broad-based research activities. Candidates appointed as Professors must hold a doctoral degree and demonstrate outstanding academic qualifications, experience in leading scientific research, the ability to provide high-quality research-based teaching and supervise theses, and evidence of international collaboration within their field. In evaluating applicants, consideration will be given to: Scientific publications and other research outputs of academic value Teaching experience and pedagogical training Participation in doctoral education Activity within the scientific community Success in securing external research funding International research experience Elected positions in international organisations Leadership and interpersonal skills. The position requires excellent Finnish language skills (C1/C2) and excellent English language skills (B2/C1). All eligibility requirements must be fulfilled by the application deadline. Position Information The position is full-time and the work location is in Helsinki, Finland. The preliminary starting salary for Assistant/Associate Professors is typically approximately €5,600-6,500 per month, and for professors, approximately €6,800-7,400 per month. The salary is based on the appointee’s qualifications and experience and can be higher than indicated in exceptional cases. At the start of the appointment, it is also possible to discuss potential start-up funding to support the launch of research activities. The position includes a six-month probationary period at the start of the employment contract. Why choose the University of Helsinki? The University of Helsinki offers an attractive career opportunity within world-class research and research-based teaching, opportunities for international collaboration, and, for candidates initially appointed as Assistant or Associate Professors, the possibility of progressing to a tenured professorship. In addition to funding opportunities available through national funding agencies, the Faculty of Science organizes annual calls for infrastructure funding and provides support in preparing international funding applications. The appointee will be supported by faculty colleagues and campus administrative and technical staff. The University of Helsinki offers occupational health services, sports facilities, opportunities for professional development, an excellent research and teaching environment, and strong support for international collaboration. Read more about working at University of Helsinki. How to apply Applications must be submitted through the University of Helsinki’s electronic recruitment system via the “Apply Now” link. Applicants currently employed by the University of Helsinki should apply through the SAP Fiori portal. The application period closes on Thursday, October 15, 2026, at 23:59 EEST (UTC +3). Applications must include the following documents in a single pdf-file, in English: An academic portfolio according to the Faculty of Science guidelines . A list of publications. Other attachments, such as recommendation letters or degree certificates, are not required at this stage. Later, candidates selected for external expert evaluation will be asked to submit their 10 most important publications. These publications should only be provided upon separate request from the Faculty. Further Information Inquiries regarding the position: Annakaisa Korja, Head of Department Tel. +358 29 415 1606 annakaisa.korja(at)helsinki.fi Technical and recruitment system inquiries: recruitment(at)helsinki.fi The Department of Geosciences and Geography at the Faculty of Science is an exceptionally diverse unit for academic research and education. Our research interest range from exploring the experiences of minorities in cities, through plate tectonics to how environments have changed since life began. The common denominator of the research at the Department is our planet Earth, from its core to the structures of its surface and its people. A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to us. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply for our positions. Click this link to read about accessibility and inclusivity at our University. JOIN US TO BUILD A BETTER WORLD – TOGETHER! #HelsinkiUniCareers Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 15.10.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Faculty of Science Sub-unit: Department of Geosciences and Geography ID: 5192 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Professors and assistant associate professors Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled Google Tag Manager Google Tag Manager is a tag management